## Step 1: Fix Stale Target And Route Override

Status:

```text
Complete locally.
Implemented in runescape-rl/fc-core/src/fc_tick.c.
Guardrails registered under the step1 CTest label.
Full local validation passed: 40/40 tests.
Training/viewer validation still requires rebuilding native binaries.
```

Goal:

```text
Fresh movement should cancel stale combat intent and stale routes.
Movement-only ticks should not auto-fire from an old target.
Explicit directional movement should not be overridden by an old approach/walk route.
```

Planned semantics:

```text
Attack only:
    select or continue target
    if range/LOS/cooldown are valid from current tile, fire
    if not valid and no explicit movement exists, approach may create/follow a route

Movement only:
    clear route_len/route_idx
    clear approach_target
    clear attack_target_idx
    move according to selected direction or tile route
    do not fire from stale target state

Attack + movement:
    resolve attack slot identity from previous observation
    check attack from pre-movement tile
    queue hit if valid
    clear approach route
    apply movement
    clear continued target intent after the attack opportunity
    require explicit future attack selection for future shots

Pending hits:
    remain independent from target clearing
```

Implementation notes:

```c
int explicit_directional_move = (act_move != FC_MOVE_IDLE);
int explicit_tile_move = (act_target_x > 0 && act_target_y > 0);
int explicit_move = explicit_directional_move || explicit_tile_move;
int explicit_attack = (act_attack > FC_ATTACK_NONE);
```

Exact ordering for Step 1:

```text
1. Detect explicit movement and explicit attack intent.
2. Clear only old stale route/approach state caused by prior ticks.
3. Process a fresh attack from the pre-movement tile if an attack was selected.
4. Build the new explicit tile route if tile movement was selected this tick.
5. Move using the new explicit tile route or directional action.
```

Reason:

```text
Old routes must not override new movement.
New explicit tile routes must not be accidentally cleared after they are built.
Attack eligibility must still be checked before movement.
```

Before auto-attack can use stale state:

```c
if (explicit_move) {
    p->route_len = 0;
    p->route_idx = 0;
    p->approach_target = 0;
    if (!explicit_attack) {
        p->attack_target_idx = -1;
    }
}
```

When selecting a fresh attack:

```c
if (explicit_attack && requested target is valid) {
    p->attack_target_idx = requested_attack_idx;
    p->approach_target = explicit_move ? 0 : 1;
}
```

After pre-movement attack evaluation:

```c
if (explicit_move) {
    p->approach_target = 0;
    /* Do not clear route_len/route_idx here after a new explicit tile route
     * has been built. Old route clearing happens before attack evaluation. */
    if (explicit_attack) {
        p->attack_target_idx = -1;
    }
}
```

Guardrails to add first:

```text
1A movement-only does not auto-fire stale target
1B queued projectile still lands after movement cancels combat intent
1C attack+move fires only from pre-movement tile
1D attack+move cannot move into range and fire
2A directional movement cancels old approach route
2B directional movement beats old walk-to-tile route
2C attack approach still works when no explicit movement is selected
```

