```

Goal:

```text
Movement and placement should check static map collision plus live entity occupancy.
```

Add shared helpers instead of scattered one-off overlap logic:

```c
void fc_build_occupancy(const FcState* state,
                        uint8_t occupied[FC_ARENA_WIDTH][FC_ARENA_HEIGHT],
                        int ignore_npc_idx,
                        int ignore_player);

int fc_footprint_available_dynamic(
    int x, int y, int size,
    const uint8_t walkable[FC_ARENA_WIDTH][FC_ARENA_HEIGHT],
    const uint8_t occupied[FC_ARENA_WIDTH][FC_ARENA_HEIGHT]);

int fc_footprint_available_for_entity(
    const FcState* state,
    int x, int y, int size,
    int moving_npc_idx,
    int ignore_player);
```

Rules:

```text
player tile blocks movement unless ignore_player is set
active non-dead NPC footprints block movement unless ignored by moving_npc_idx
the moving NPC must ignore its own current footprint
start-of-tick footprints remain reserved for the movement pass
diagonal movement must check final, horizontal intermediate, and vertical intermediate footprints
LOS remains based on static map collision
```

Static and dynamic collision must be separate concepts:

```text
static collision:
    walls, rocks, cave obstacles, cave boundaries

dynamic collision:
    player tile
    live NPC footprints
    reserved start-of-tick footprints
```

Start-of-tick reservation rule:

```text
Treat every live entity's starting footprint as blocked for the duration of the movement pass.
This prevents same-tick body-swap behavior where NPC A moves into NPC B's old tile
while NPC B moves into NPC A's old tile.
```

Add dynamic-aware sized pathing, not only final destination checks:

```c
int fc_move_toward_dynamic(...);
int fc_npc_step_toward_sized_dynamic(...);
int fc_pathfind_bfs_sized_dynamic(...);
```

Requirements:

```text
BFS/pathfinding candidates must reject terrain-blocked tiles.
BFS/pathfinding candidates must reject occupied or reserved footprints.
Large NPC BFS must validate the full footprint at every candidate step.
Diagonal BFS/path steps must reject dynamic corner clipping, not only static corner clipping.
Do not only check the final route destination; every route step must be valid.
```

