## Step 4: Replace Greedy NPC Movement With RSMod-Style Player-Bounds Chase

Status:

```text
Complete locally.
Implemented in runescape-rl/fc-core/include/fc_npc.h.
Implemented in runescape-rl/fc-core/include/fc_pathfinding.h.
Implemented in runescape-rl/fc-core/src/fc_npc.c.
Implemented in runescape-rl/fc-core/src/fc_pathfinding.c.
Guardrails registered under the step4 CTest label.
Full local validation passed: 55/55 tests.
Follow-up correction: removed global attack-position search after RSMod/2009scape
audit showed it was too smart for OSRS-like NPC chase. NPCs now chase the
player's live bounds using a naive pathing-entity destination and one validated
dynamic step per tick.
Viewer rebuilt against updated fc-core.
Training validation still requires rebuilding the native PufferLib backend before the next run.
```

Goal:

```text
NPCs should attack only when their current footprint can already attack.
If they cannot attack, they should chase the player's live bounds, matching
RSMod's `RouteRequestPathingEntity` / `naiveDestination` behavior, instead of
globally searching for a better LOS/ranged firing tile.
```

Add current-position attack helper:

```c
int fc_npc_position_can_attack_player(
    const FcState* state,
    const FcNpc* npc,
    int candidate_x,
    int candidate_y);
```

Behavior:

```text
if NPC can attack from current footprint:
    stay and attack/wait for cooldown

if NPC cannot attack:
    compute the naive pathing-entity destination around the player's bounds
    take one dynamic, full-footprint validated step toward that destination

Do not pathfind/search for a separate ranged/magic LOS firing tile.
```

Attack-position rules:

```text
melee NPCs need valid adjacent melee contact
ranged/magic NPCs need range and static LOS
Tok-Xil/Ket-Zek/Jad may melee when adjacent if their mechanics allow it
large NPC chase movement must fit the full footprint at the direct step
large NPC chase movement must reject occupied/reserved start-of-tick footprints
```

Large-footprint chase requirement:

```text
When a large NPC steps while chasing, validate the whole top-left footprint.
Do not choose or validate movement by center point alone.
The direct step is valid only if every tile in the NPC footprint is statically
walkable and dynamically unoccupied/unreserved.
```

